# Reference Point — Subsection Eyebrow (`.eyebrow.soft`)

When the user says **"reference point"** for a grey uppercase section label (e.g. "Chatbot placement", "About the project"), match `p.eyebrow.soft` inside `.overview-sub-head` in `#overview`, `#discovery`, or `#ai-layer`.

## Structure

```html
<div class="overview-sub-head stack-16">
  <p class="eyebrow soft">Section label</p>
  <h3 class="title">Headline below</h3>
</div>
```

Standalone label only — pair with `h3.title` per `reference-point-sub-head.mdc` / `reference-point-sub-title.mdc`.

## Visual spec

| Property | Value |
|----------|-------|
| Element | `p.eyebrow.soft` |
| Font | `var(--sans)` (Instrument Sans, inherited from body) |
| Size | `var(--label-size)` → **0.875rem (14px)** |
| Weight | **500** |
| Letter-spacing | **0.2em** |
| Transform | **uppercase** |
| Color | `var(--label-soft)` → **#9ca3af** |
| Margin | 0 (default reset) |

Scoped selectors (identical treatment):

```css
.overview-section .overview-sub-head .eyebrow.soft,
#discovery .overview-sub-head .eyebrow.soft,
#ai-layer .overview-sub-head .eyebrow.soft,
.hybrid-chat-head .eyebrow.soft
```

Parent wrapper `.overview-sub-head.stack-16` uses `gap: 0.75rem` in `#ai-layer` (1rem elsewhere in overview).

## vs other eyebrows

| Context | Class | Color | Weight |
|---------|-------|-------|--------|
| Main section | `.eyebrow` | brown `var(--label)` | 600 |
| **Subsection (this reference)** | **`.eyebrow.soft`** | **grey `#9ca3af`** | **500** |
| Hybrid chat head | `.hybrid-chat-head .eyebrow.soft` | same — shared selector |
| Role card | `.role-card .eyebrow` | `#6b7280` | — |

## Do not

- Use brown `.eyebrow` for subsection labels — always add `.soft`.
- Use `.g-label` or `.col-label` — different components with different colors/sizes.
- Bump weight to 600 — subsection eyebrows stay at 500.
- Apply inline styles — use the shared class only.
